From 5146e2d2e467a93077ab0523046b1d2fc3d8ca7e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 25 Jun 2026 07:18:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] patch 0257 -- gus SFX (#38): fx6e host-crash sub-step
 instrumentation + host-heap trace + RENDERSAFE pre-render guard

iter-1 (wave-gussfx1) localized the #38 GUS-SFX quit-to-DOS to the
HOST-side render of slot 110 / fx6e: the engine DEBUG.LOG ends at
"fx6d DONE ... next slot..." and the post-loop summary never prints,
so the fault is in fx6e's load() -> render() -> sign-flip, BEFORE any
GF1 upload (the upload+playback path is proven working on g2k: 68 game
uploads + 86 probe triggers). The pre-0257 first per-slot diag fired
only AFTER render + sign-flip, so a crash in load()/render() left no
log naming the sub-step.

Engine-side audit REFUTED all three data-driven suspects: every .pxt
size field is <= 62KB (no 32-bit nsamples overflow), fx6e is a normal
1-channel/4000-sample sound, and synth()/the render mix-loop/the sign-
flip are all provably in-bounds for the real data. The crash signature
(moves fx6d->fx6e when prior guards shift heap layout; faults at fx6e's
first malloc after "fx6d DONE") is the HEAP-CORRUPTION / host-memory /
DPMI-page class -- the corruptor is likely not fx6e itself. So this
patch is OBSERVABILITY-FIRST; it does not guess a fix.

Instrumentation (GUS_DIAG-gated, init-time, memory-only -- zero GF1
port reads):
  * Per-slot breadcrumbs now fire BEFORE load, AFTER load, and AFTER
    render (final_size + max_nsamples). They flush per-line (patch
    0036), so the last line on disk after a quit-to-DOS names the exact
    crashing sub-step on the next g2k swap.
  * The BEFORE-load breadcrumb also samples DJGPP host-heap state --
    mallinfo() uordblks/fordblks/arena + sbrk(0) (program break) -- at
    the steady-state point (prior iteration's freeBuf already ran). A
    monotonic climb across the ~109 slots toward fx6e would reveal a
    leak/heap-exhaustion corruptor; a flat trace refutes it and points
    the corruptor outside Pixtone. DJGPP provides mallinfo (libc symbol
    _mallinfo) but only via the internal <libc/malldbg.h> without an
    extern "C" wrapper, so the minimal slice is redeclared here at C
    linkage to resolve the call.

Adds opt-in killswitch SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_GUS_SFX_RENDERSAFE (strict "1",
default OFF = byte-identical to pre-0257): when ON, the music-priority
budget cap is hoisted to AFTER load() but BEFORE render(), so a slot
that cannot fit the remaining SFX budget is skipped WITHOUT rendering.
Upload SELECTION is unchanged (same final_size budget decision, computed
pre-render from the just-parsed nsamples); only the doomed slot's
host-side render() is skipped. fx6e is over-budget after fx6d (~2.3KB
left, needs 4000B) so it is budget-skipped today anyway -- but only
AFTER its render runs. RENDERSAFE skips that render. Same-binary A/B:
OFF reproduces the fx6e crash; ON survives IFF the fault is inside
render() (vs load()), which the breadcrumbs disambiguate. NOT a proven
mechanism -- a correct robustness guard + a sharper observability A/B.

DOS-specific: the crash is DPMI-page-dependent (host quit-to-DOS, no
LOG_CRITICAL) and only reproduces on the real PicoGUS /mode gus --
DOSBox-X cannot reproduce it. Only consulted under AUDIO_BACKEND=gus.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/sound/Pixtone.cpp | 114 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 114 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/sound/Pixtone.cpp b/src/sound/Pixtone.cpp
index e9816e5f..f7427a15 100644
--- a/src/sound/Pixtone.cpp
+++ b/src/sound/Pixtone.cpp
@@ -22,6 +22,23 @@
 
 #ifdef __DJGPP__
 #include <dpmi.h>  // patch 0167 (Lever 3): _go32_dpmi_lock_data for raw_master_buf DPMI lock
+#include <unistd.h>  // patch 0257 (#38 iter-2): sbrk(0) -- program break / heap top witness
+// patch 0257 (#38 iter-2): DJGPP host-heap-state breadcrumbs for the GUS-SFX
+// fx6e crash triage. DJGPP DOES provide mallinfo() (symbol _mallinfo in libc.a),
+// but its declaration lives in the internal <libc/malldbg.h> WITHOUT an
+// `extern "C"` wrapper -- including it from C++ would mangle the call and fail
+// to link. So declare the minimal slice we need ourselves, at C linkage, so the
+// call resolves to libc's _mallinfo. The struct layout matches malldbg.h's
+// `struct mallinfo` (10 ints); uordblks = heap bytes in use, fordblks = free,
+// arena = total managed. GUS_DIAG-gated, init-time, memory-only (honors the
+// PicoGUS hard rules: zero GF1 port reads). See team-lead heap-theory ask.
+extern "C" {
+  struct mallinfo {
+    int arena, ordblks, smblks, hblks, hblkhd, usmblks, fsmblks,
+        uordblks, fordblks, keepcost;
+  };
+  struct mallinfo mallinfo(void);
+}
 #endif
 #include <cmath>
 #include <cstdint>
@@ -600,6 +617,34 @@ bool Pixtone::initGusSfx()
   // upload-len BEFORE its upload so a crash log's last line names the culprit.
   const char *_gd = SDL_GetHint("SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_GUS_DIAG");
   const bool _gusdiag = _gd && _gd[0] == '1' && _gd[1] == '\0';
+  // patch 0257 (#38 iter-2): GUS_SFX_RENDERSAFE -- opt-in (strict "1", default OFF
+  // = byte-identical to pre-0257). When ON, the music-priority budget cap is
+  // hoisted to AFTER load() but BEFORE render(): a slot whose predicted upload
+  // length (== final_size == max enabled-channel nsamples, floored at the 64-byte
+  // topbuf min) cannot fit the remaining SFX budget is skipped WITHOUT rendering.
+  // The upload SELECTION is identical to the existing post-render cap below (same
+  // final_size decision, computed pre-render from the just-parsed nsamples); the
+  // only difference is the doomed slot's host-side render() is not run.
+  //
+  // WHY (iter-1 / wave-gussfx1 result): the #38 crash is HOST-side in the render
+  // of slot 110/fx6e -- the engine log ends at "fx6d DONE ... next slot..." and
+  // fx6e's first per-slot line never prints. fx6e is over-budget after fx6d
+  // (~2.3KB left, fx6e needs 4000B), so it is budget-skipped anyway today -- but
+  // only AFTER its render runs. RENDERSAFE skips that render. A/B on the SAME
+  // binary: OFF reproduces the fx6e crash; ON survives IF the fault is inside
+  // render() (vs load()). Combined with the per-substep instrumentation below
+  // (before-load / after-load / after-render, GUS_DIAG-gated) the g2k swap pins
+  // the exact crashing sub-step. THIS IS NOT A CONFIRMED ROOT-CAUSE FIX: the
+  // audit found NO in-path out-of-bounds write for the (sane) .pxt data -- every
+  // slot's size <= 62KB (no 32-bit nsamples overflow), fx6e is a normal
+  // 1-channel/4000-sample sound, and synth()/the render mix-loop/the sign-flip
+  // are all provably in-bounds. So this is a correct robustness guard + a sharper
+  // observability A/B, NOT a proven mechanism. See docs/internal/GUS-SFX-38-HANDOFF.md.
+  const char *_rs = SDL_GetHint("SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_GUS_SFX_RENDERSAFE");
+  const bool _rendersafe = _rs && _rs[0] == '1' && _rs[1] == '\0';
+  LOG_INFO("gus SFX rendersafe [nx0257]: {} (SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_GUS_SFX_RENDERSAFE; "
+           "opt-in pre-render budget skip; per-substep load/render instrumentation "
+           "rides on GUS_DIAG).", _rendersafe ? "ON" : "OFF (default)");
   std::string path = ResourceManager::getInstance()->getPathForDir("pxt/");
   int uploaded = 0, failed = 0, skipped = 0;
   uint32_t sfx_used = 0;
@@ -617,9 +662,78 @@ bool Pixtone::initGusSfx()
     std::ostringstream filename;
     filename << path << "fx" << std::hex << std::setw(2) << std::setfill('0') << slot << ".pxt";
     stPXSound snd;
+    // patch 0257 (#38 iter-2): per-substep instrumentation (GUS_DIAG-gated, init-
+    // time, memory-only). Pre-0257 the FIRST per-slot line fired only AFTER render
+    // + sign-flip, so a crash in load()/render() left NO log naming the slot (the
+    // fx6e fault is exactly this case). These breadcrumbs -- before-load,
+    // after-load, after-render -- flush per-line (patch 0036) so the LAST line on
+    // disk after a quit-to-DOS names the exact crashing sub-step.
+    if (_gusdiag)
+    {
+      // patch 0257 (#38 iter-2): host-heap-state at the BEFORE-load point. The
+      // prior iteration's snd.freeBuf() already ran (loop tail), so this samples
+      // the STEADY-STATE heap with no transient render buffers resident -- a
+      // monotonic climb of uordblks (in-arena leak) or brk (sbrk growth) across
+      // the ~109 slots toward fx6e is the heap-exhaustion/leak signature the lead
+      // wants this swap to decide. mallinfo() is sampled BEFORE LOG_INFO formats
+      // (whose own transient allocs are freed by the next slot's sample), so the
+      // cross-slot delta is clean. The audit found NO live per-slot leak on the
+      // gus path (initGusSfx never calls _prepareToPlay, so resampled[]/chunk/
+      // raw_master_buf stay null; snd is a value re-freeBuf'd each iteration) --
+      // so the expectation is a FLAT trace, which would REFUTE heap-exhaustion
+      // and point the corruptor outside Pixtone (DPMI/CWSDPMI page commit, or a
+      // non-Pixtone engine alloc). A climb would reveal a leak the audit missed.
+#ifdef __DJGPP__
+      struct mallinfo _mi  = mallinfo();
+      const unsigned    _brk = (unsigned)(uintptr_t)sbrk(0);
+      LOG_INFO("gus SFX diag: fx{:02x} (slot {}) BEFORE load '{}' [host-heap: "
+               "uordblks={} fordblks={} arena={} brk=0x{:x}]...", slot, slot,
+               filename.str(), _mi.uordblks, _mi.fordblks, _mi.arena, _brk);
+#else
+      LOG_INFO("gus SFX diag: fx{:02x} (slot {}) BEFORE load '{}'...", slot, slot,
+               filename.str());
+#endif
+    }
     if (!snd.load(filename.str()))
       continue;
+    if (_gusdiag)
+      LOG_INFO("gus SFX diag: fx{:02x} load OK -- computing render budget...", slot);
+
+    // patch 0257 (#38 iter-2): RENDERSAFE pre-render budget skip. final_size after
+    // render == max(enabled-channel nsamples, 64). Predict it from the just-loaded
+    // nsamples (load() populated them) and skip render of any slot that cannot fit
+    // the remaining music-priority budget. Same upload SELECTION as the post-render
+    // cap below; only the doomed slot's render() is skipped. freeBuf() here is safe
+    // (load set channels[].buffer = nullptr; render/allocBuf was never called).
+    if (_rendersafe)
+    {
+      uint32_t _pred = 64u;  // allocBuf() topbufsize floor
+      for (int ci = 0; ci < PXT_NO_CHANNELS; ++ci)
+        if (snd.channels[ci].enabled && snd.channels[ci].nsamples > _pred)
+          _pred = snd.channels[ci].nsamples;
+      if (sfx_used + _pred > sfx_budget)
+      {
+        ++skipped;
+        if (_gusdiag)
+          LOG_INFO("gus SFX diag: fx{:02x} RENDERSAFE pre-render SKIP (pred_size={} "
+                   "sfx_used={} budget={}); render NOT run.", slot, (unsigned)_pred,
+                   (unsigned)sfx_used, (unsigned)sfx_budget);
+        snd.freeBuf();
+        continue;
+      }
+    }
+
     snd.render();  // -> final_buffer: 8-bit SIGNED mono @ 22050 Hz, final_size bytes
+    if (_gusdiag)
+    {
+      uint32_t _maxns = 0;
+      for (int ci = 0; ci < PXT_NO_CHANNELS; ++ci)
+        if (snd.channels[ci].enabled && snd.channels[ci].nsamples > _maxns)
+          _maxns = snd.channels[ci].nsamples;
+      LOG_INFO("gus SFX diag: fx{:02x} render OK (final_size={} max_nsamples={}) -- "
+               "sign-flipping + uploading...", slot, (unsigned)snd.final_size,
+               (unsigned)_maxns);
+    }
 
     if (snd.final_buffer && snd.final_size > 0)
     {
-- 
